  "product_code": "BASLUS-00005",
  "question_extra": [
    "## Follow-up research question",
    "",
    "The previous job (`inputs/prior/rayman-prior-e3ea73ec.tgz`; read its `handoff.md` and `field-ledger.md` first) confirmed the slot header (`SC 13 01`), filename at 0xb, completion ASCII at 0xf, continues at 0x200 and lives at 0x400. The editor field map in `inputs/spec.json` for cages, powers (0x300/0x301), current level (0x1080) and level unlocks (0x280..0x297) does **not** match real USA saves. Treat every editor offset as an unconfirmed hypothesis.",
    "",
    "Answer, with native evidence:",
    "",
    "1. Where are cages freed recorded, per level (6 per level, 102 total)? Give offset/bit per cage or the encoding, and how the per-level count is derived.",
    "2. Where are the unlocked powers (fist, hang, helicopter, grab, run/super-helicopter) stored, and what bit/value means each?",
    "3. Where are the current level / map position and the map unlocks stored?",
    "4. What checksum protects the slot (candidate: the last 4 bytes, `31 87 5f 6d` in the GameFAQs save)? Identify coverage and algorithm, and prove it by editing a byte, fixing the checksum, and having the game accept the save; and showing it rejects a broken one. If you cannot establish it, record it as unconfirmed with the experiments tried. Never mark an invented checksum as passing.",
    "",
    "Leads from a static look at the GameFAQs save (unverified): byte 0x2D0 = 0x64; 0x1088-0x10EF hold 0x0001 words; populated ranges 0x340-0x3FF, 0x1000-0x1330 and 0x1610-0x16F0.",
    "",
    "Method: unwrap the DexDrive `.gme` (`inputs/saves/rayman-gamefaqs-100.gme`) onto a disposable virtual card, load it natively and record the on-screen percent, map and cage counts. Then create your own progressed saves from a new game (fresh file; after freeing one cage; after freeing all six in Pink Plant Woods; after gaining a power; after reaching a new map node) and diff consecutive slots so each change is attributable to one in-game event. Where feasible, confirm a hypothesis by editing the byte(s), fixing any checksum, loading natively and observing the change. Synthetic edits stay labelled synthetic.",
    "",
    "Deliverables under `outputs/`:",
    "- `outputs/field-ledger.md`: every field with offset, encoding, evidence IDs and status `confirmed-native`, `confirmed-diff`, `synthetic-only` or `unconfirmed`.",
    "- `outputs/decoder/`: updated read-only decoder (start from the prior `decoder/rayman.py`), its test suite, and a runnable test command; unconfirmed fields must decode as unknown/null, not as editor guesses.",
    "- `outputs/fixtures/`: the in-emulator saves (raw 8 KiB slot bytes, no BIOS/disc), each with a JSON sidecar of the natively observed state (percent, level, cages, powers). Do not republish the GameFAQs save bytes; cite it by sha256.",
    "- `outputs/research.json` with validation entries for each required check id.",
    "",
    "Check ids: `field-ledger` passes when the ledger exists and covers all target fields with a status; `decoder-suite` passes when the decoder tests run green against the fixtures; `progress-distinct` passes when at least two native snapshots decode to different summaries; `native-load` as defined above.",
    "",
    "## Closeout contract (read carefully)",
    "",
    "Only these `outputs/result.json` outcome/reason pairs are valid: `complete`/`scope_complete`; `partial`/`budget_exhausted`; `partial`/`user_requested`; `blocked`/`no_actionable_work` (with non-empty `blockers`). Any other pair is rejected and the job is marked failed. If some questions are answered and others are stuck (for example the checksum), report **`partial` with `budget_exhausted`**, list the open items in `blockers`, and keep all evidence. Use `blocked` only when no permitted work at all remains. `complete` requires every required check to be `passed` in `outputs/research.json`."
  ],
